# Generated 2026-10-26
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 318)
#
# Doc 24 stage 2 (the image handlers). Patch 315 built the channel
# (BITMAPF_OPACITY, flag bits 16-23), the content_redraw_data.opacity
# carrier and the fold in all four handlers that call the bitmap op
# (image.c, bmp.c, nssprite.c, rsvg.c) -- but only the background sites
# filled the carrier, so an <img> inside an opacity group painted solid,
# and a SCALED faded bitmap drew solid too (doc 24's open fork).
#
#  - redraw.c: the object paint site fills obj_data.opacity from
#    html_redraw_group_opacity_byte() (0 when the group is full, so solid
#    pages' flags are unchanged). Image handlers fold it already; HTML
#    and text contents ignore the field. Every other content_redraw_data
#    constructor (content.c thumbnails, browser_window.c -- a standalone
#    image document --, print.c, treeview.c) still sets 0 (solid).
#  - frontends/vita: a scaled tile at a partial bucket now draws a copy of
#    its texture with every alpha byte scaled by the bucket alpha
#    (vita_bitmap_faded_texture, bitmap.c) through the same
#    vita2d_draw_texture_scale -- doc 24's recommended device-safe
#    default: no stub entry both scales and tints, and the copy needs
#    none. Straight alpha, so scaling the alpha byte is the whole fade:
#    (a * A) / 255, the arithmetic the sim's tint_part uses for the 1:1
#    path, so 1:1 and scaled fades read the same pixels. The copy comes
#    from the texture pool and goes straight onto the dead list, so its
#    memory is only reused after the frame the GPU is drawing retires
#    (vita_bitmap_frame_retired) -- the GPU may still sample it this
#    frame. A one-entry memo (source, alpha) copies once when the same
#    image is drawn twice at one alpha in a frame; repeat tiles share the
#    op's copy. No copy is made for a draw that cannot reach the clip. A
#    refused allocation draws solid and is counted (log: "bitmaps: N
#    faded copies (K KB), M refused" at load end, only when non-zero, so
#    solid pages' logs are unchanged); the trace then reads solid too.
#    The tint_part 1:1 path and bucket-0 skip are unchanged. Stage 3
